// The workspace exists so that drive/ can be a real module WITHOUT a
// replace in go.mod. That distinction is the whole point: `go install
// pkg@version` refuses a module whose go.mod carries replace
// directives, and `go run github.com/incantery/vera/cmd/vera@latest` is
// the first line of the README — the on-ramp that promises one binary,
// no install, no account. A replace would have quietly cost that.
//
// So the published requirement is an ordinary pseudo-version, and this
// file — which consumers never see, and which pkg@version ignores —
// points local builds at ./drive so edits there are picked up without
// a push round-trip. After changing drive/, `go get
// github.com/incantery/vera/drive@<commit>` is what makes the change
// real for everyone else.
go 1.25.8

use (
	.
	./drive
	../mote
)
